; --- The two fences ---------------------------------------------------------------
; ⚠️ ONE INTERACTABLE EACH (a DialogueComponent), trade behind DialogueEffect.OpenShop — 38E's rule,
; and it applies here for 38E's reason: GetComponent<T> returns the first child match, so a
; VendorComponent stacked on a talking merchant is a component that never fires. Both of these have
; conversations worth protecting, so both take the dialogue route.
;
; ⚠️ NO NEW BODIES. Sedge wears npc_hooded — the same hood the gate-hand wears at the Crossway, and
; that echo is deliberate: they are the same trade on opposite sides of the same road. Coyle wears
; npc_merchant_m. Neither wears npc_townsman (a hi-vis vest and a hard hat) or npc_merchant_f (a
; t-shirt and trainers); both are retired, and the second one took three sub-phases to catch.
[node name="Sedge" type="Node3D" parent="."]
